   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Key dates in Spain",
     "texto": [
      "- **Nochebuena**, 24 December: many families have a long dinner.\n- **Navidad**, 25 December.\n- **Nochevieja**, 31 December: people eat twelve **uvas**, one with each chime at midnight.\n- **Reyes Magos**, 6 January: on that day children receive presents.\n\nFor a birthday you say **¡Feliz cumpleaños!** or **¡Felicidades!** There is a **tarta** with **velas**.\n\nThe verbs: **celebrar** a birthday; **invitar** someone to a party; **regalar** something to someone; **brindar** to something: ¡salud!"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Invitar, regalar and brindar",
     "texto": [
      "These verbs take a fixed small word:\n\n- **invitar a** someone **a** something: **te invito a mi fiesta**.\n- **regalar** something **a** someone: the person who receives the gift is said with **le** or **les**: **le regalo una tarta a Lucía**.\n- **brindar por** something: **brindamos por tu cumpleaños**.\n- **celebrar** something, with no small word: **celebro mi cumpleaños**.\n\nFor a near plan we use **ir a + infinitive**: **vamos a brindar**."
     ],
